0.25 0.15 (to the memory manager requesting a page allocation and the binary code to fill the) 124.72 435.49 B
-0.21 (pages with. With this allocation scheme it is easy to load the rest of the kernel since the) 124.72 423.49 P
0.25 0.05 (binaries are specified on creation. The boot loader can load the core and then start to) 124.72 411.49 B
-0.06 (load the rest of the kernel using the core. As soon as enough of the kernel is loaded the) 124.72 399.49 P
(boot loader can terminate.) 124.72 387.49 T
