0.25 0.12 (In the cases where you have a manager in the core and an advanced manager in the) 124.72 693.49 B
-0.08 (kernel it is vital that there is a clear definition of what should be done in the kernel and) 124.72 681.49 P
0.25 0.14 (what should be done in the core. In our view the core should only manage the very) 124.72 669.49 B
0.25 0.39 (basic things, leaving all policy decisions and more complicated services to the) 124.72 657.49 B
0.25 0.31 (advanced managers in the kernel layer. Consequently, the core process manager) 124.72 645.49 B
0.06 (should only manage the creation of new process control blocks and run a process until) 124.72 633.49 P
0.25 0.06 (it yields or falls asleep on some operation. When a process is removed from the run-) 124.72 621.49 B
0.25 0.19 (queue, a new process will be selected to run. The most basic run-queues \050running,) 124.72 609.49 B
0.25 0.04 (blocked, and ready\051 should be managed, but it should also be possible to create other) 124.72 597.49 B
0.08 (queues and move processes between the queues on command from the advanced serv-) 124.72 585.49 P
-0.12 (ices. The advanced process manager should maintain these extra queues and command) 124.72 573.49 P
0.25 0.11 (movement of processes according to its algorithms. Creating a process at the kernel) 124.72 561.49 B
0.25 0.02 (level can also include more than one operation in the core. Memory may be allocated) 124.72 549.49 B
0.25 0.13 (and communications channels set up, according to the advanced process manager\325s) 124.72 537.49 B
(strategies.) 124.72 525.49 T
