-0.12 (A distributed file system is accessed through a certain mount point, which is a separate) 124.72 663.49 P
0.25 0.05 (file agent. This mount point agent will act as a bridge to the remote system, showing) 124.72 651.49 B
-0.07 (the contents of the remote directory as if it existed on the local disk. All file operations) 124.72 639.49 P
-0.23 (come through the communications manager, so the file system manager need not know) 124.72 627.49 P
0.25 0.07 (whether it is a request from another computer or a local request that it is processing.) 124.72 615.49 B
0.25 0.02 (The actual directory agent that is accessed via the mount point agent decides whether) 124.72 603.49 B
0.25 0.25 (to accept or to refuse access from a certain host or mount point. The causes for a) 124.72 591.49 B
0.19 (refusal can be anything from not being on a trusted network to a temporary lockout to) 124.72 579.49 P
(perform system management or backups.) 124.72 567.49 T
