0.25 0 (The agent file system described above gives enormous flexibility, since each file may) 124.72 527.49 B
0.25 0.08 (have unique behaviour. You also reduce the need for specific programs traditionally) 124.72 515.49 B
0.25 0.07 (needed to manage the files. Since the files carry their own behaviour they can easily) 124.72 503.49 B
0.25 0.18 (move to a new host within the network or even a completely different host system) 124.72 491.49 B
(\050running ABOS\051 on another network and still execute in their intended way.) 124.72 479.49 T
0.25 0.04 (Having each file handling its own security and behaviour, and also the decision right) 124.72 461.49 B
-0.12 (concerning who should be allowed to do what, gives an extensible security model. The) 124.72 449.49 P
0.25 0.05 (file agent will not allow the file to be transported to an insecure host, nor will it give) 124.72 437.49 B
0.25 0.02 (data to an unauthorized client. The file agent can also choose to show different views) 124.72 425.49 B
0.25 0.06 (of the file to different clients in accordance to their specific security status. The files) 124.72 413.49 B
0.25 0.17 (can also decide for themselves whether to encrypt the data or not. Letting the files) 124.72 401.49 B
-0.02 (manage this by themselves removes the need for the file system manager to know spe-) 124.72 389.49 P
0.25 0.01 (cifics about every file. Different encryption algorithms can be used for different files,) 124.72 377.49 B
0.25 0.14 (improving performance on files with low demands on encryption compared to files) 124.72 365.49 B
(with high demands.) 124.72 353.49 T
0.25 0.05 (By letting each file agent manage its own caching mechanisms, file performance can) 124.72 335.49 B
0.25 0.04 (to some extent be tuned for the individual systems. The main disadvantage regarding) 124.72 323.49 B
0.25 0.1 (performance is that for each file request where the file agent is not already active, a) 124.72 311.49 B
0.25 0.18 (new process will have to be created and the request forwarded via IPC. Removing) 124.72 299.49 B
0.25 0.12 (some of the autonomicity of the files, reducing them to mere threads within the file) 124.72 287.49 B
0.25 0.01 (system manager can reduce this bottleneck. To achieve better fault tolerance, one can) 124.72 275.49 B
0.25 0.14 (have a set of file-agent nurseries that each takes care of a number of agent threads.) 124.72 263.49 B
0.25 0.04 (These nursery agents can quickly optimize their numbers with regards to the average) 124.72 251.49 B
-0.05 (number of file requests so that there are no more nursery agents than are needed at any) 124.72 239.49 P
(given time.) 124.72 227.49 T
0.25 0.06 (The mount point agent provides possibilities for redundant systems, letting the agent) 124.72 209.49 B
0.04 (determine which file system to provide access to from a set of choices. If one server is) 124.72 197.49 P
-0.03 (down, the agent points to the next one. It can also dynamically determine the fastest of) 124.72 185.49 P
0 (a set of servers, and let the request go to this one. If the mounted file system is not just) 124.72 173.49 P
0.25 0.05 (a read-only file system but is updated as well, the servers should of course work as a) 124.72 161.49 B
