0.25 0.09 (Traditionally the structure of the operating system is static, and applications need to) 124.72 301.49 B
0.25 0.03 (adjust to this structure. In some cases this implies a trade-off between what you want) 124.72 289.49 B
0.25 0.15 (to do and what the operating system allows. ABOS allows developers to adjust the) 124.72 277.49 B
0.25 0.02 (operating system kernel to the applications running on it, while still being able to run) 124.72 265.49 B
(more than one program concurrently.) 124.72 253.49 T
-0.12 (The service layer adds a new conceptual category of software; applications that are not) 124.72 235.49 P
0.22 (part of the kernel tasks but still a part of the operating system. To have a special layer) 124.72 223.49 P
0.17 (for these ensures that they are not involved in the kernel, but is still treated differently) 124.72 211.49 P
(compared to user applications with regards to security and scheduling.) 124.72 199.49 T
